# Block-Merger Determinism — Formal Verification (merge algebra)
#
# Mechanizes the consensus-critical DETERMINISM of the F1R3FLY block merger and
# the algebra of its per-channel / event-log combine operators. Mirrors the
# fork-choice and finalized-floor developments (axiom-free, Stdlib-only).
#
# Properties, and what each rules out (all are no-fork / merge-soundness):
#   * KeepOneOrder (P3) - the 5-key DeployChainIndex comparator is a STRICT TOTAL
#     order whose Equal-class is EXACTLY the injective terminal key, so the merge
#     winner is node-identical. STRICTLY FIRMER than fork_choice/TieBreak.v: NO
#     NoDup / hash-distinctness premise (the injective key makes distinct entries
#     orderable BY CONSTRUCTION).
#   * ChannelNetting (GAP-1) - ChannelChange.combine is commutative; the shipped
#     max-union operator is NON-associative (Finding A, EXHIBITED as a theorem,
#     mirror of IntegerAdd.launder_exhibit); the sum-union FIX is a commutative
#     monoid whose fold is permutation-invariant (order-independent netting).
#   * ConflictSoundness (GAP-3) - the REMOVED single-value-cell (consume-then-
#     produce) conflict predicate is SUBSUMED by the retained double-consume race
#     detector, except on number/foldable channels (intrinsically mergeable).
#   * EventLogSplit (P2) - the user/system EventLogIndex split is a set-union
#     semilattice: combine(fold user, fold system) = fold all, so conflict
#     detection on the split index equals detection on the monolithic index.
#   * MainTheorem - four end-to-end capstones, each `exact`-discharged from its
#     module, introducing NO new assumptions.
#
# Source under verification:
#   casper/src/rust/merging/deploy_chain_index.rs            (impl Ord, 5-key tower)
#   rspace++/src/rspace/merger/channel_change.rs             (combine / vec_union)
#   rspace++/src/rspace/merger/merging_logic.rs              (conflicts detectors)
#   rspace++/src/rspace/merger/event_log_index.rs            (combine, split fold)
#
# Zero `Admitted`. No custom `Axiom` or `Parameter`. Section `Variable`s
# (KeepOneOrder g1..g4; ConflictSoundness is_number_ch) are PARAMETERS of the
# closed term, not axioms and not constraining hypotheses.
#
# Module dependency graph (-> = "depends on"):
#   KeepOneOrder      (standalone: lexicographic 5-key strict total order)
#   ChannelNetting    (standalone: multiset combine algebra + Finding A exhibit)
#   ConflictSoundness (standalone: removed-predicate subsumption)
#   EventLogSplit     (standalone: set-union semilattice split)
#   MainTheorem -> all four (capstones, axiom-free)

